# Field Sales/Marketer Rep Tracking Apps — Feature Research

Scoping reference for a tablet app that tracks marketers/sales reps in real time: location, activities, tasks, goals, and zones. Compiled from public product/feature pages of the leading players in the "field force management / field sales tracking / retail execution" category, July 2026.

## Category names to search under
This product category goes by several names depending on the vendor: **field force management**, **field sales tracking / sales force automation (SFA)**, **retail execution**, and **field employee GPS tracking**. All converge on the same core feature set.

## Master feature list (consolidated across all products)

### 1. Real-time location tracking
- Live map view of all reps' current position ("Find My Team" / live dashboard)
- GPS breadcrumbs / trails — full path traveled through the day, replayable
- Location history and route-travelled visualization
- Distance-traveled reports, battery/network status of the rep's device

### 2. Geofencing & zone/territory management
- Draw custom virtual boundaries (polygons, multi-coordinate) around stores, client sites, or whole territories
- Geo-verified check-in/check-out — rep can only clock in or log a visit while physically inside the geofence
- Geofence-violation tracking and real-time deviation alerts when a rep strays off-plan
- Territory/zone assignment per rep, with territory-wise performance reporting
- AI/route-optimized "beat plans" — auto-generated daily visit sequences within a zone

### 3. Task & goal assignment
- Assign one-off or recurring tasks to specific reps, with priority and due dates
- Tasks can be auto-allocated by proximity, skill set, and availability
- Individual and team goal/target-setting (visits, sales value, KPIs), with a "Target vs Achievement" report
- Checklists and structured forms attached to tasks/visits
- Automated follow-up/corrective-action tasks when something fails

### 4. Visit & activity tracking
- One-tap check-in/check-out per visit, time- and location-stamped
- Activity logging beyond location: calls, meetings, notes, visit outcomes, competitor mentions
- "Remote check-in" for off-site work (admin, training) that isn't tied to a geofence
- Photo capture with annotation attached to a visit/task (proof of visit, shelf audits)
- AI photo recognition for shelf-share/planogram/compliance audits (retail-specific)
- Voice notes / speech-to-text for field data entry

### 5. Route planning & optimization
- Auto-optimized daily route across assigned visits (reduces drive time)
- Manual route/territory drawing on a map, then optimize
- Coverage-gap analysis — flags under-served parts of a territory

### 6. Attendance
- Automated or manual check-in/out tied to workday templates
- Geo-verified attendance (can't mark present unless inside the zone)
- Face-recognition attendance (anti-spoofing)
- Leave management

### 7. Order, expense & proof capture
- In-app order booking / product catalog with custom pricing & discounts
- Expense/mileage capture with receipt photo, multi-level approval workflows, role-based spend caps
- Digital signature capture for agreements

### 8. Reporting & manager dashboards
- Real-time dashboard: task completion rates, visit compliance, cross-team performance
- Rep and team leaderboards (activities, appointments, deals closed)
- KPI framework typically 3 layers: **Activity** (visits/calls made), **Execution** (quality of the visit), **Outcome** (revenue/growth per territory)
- Drill-down reports per store/district/rep

### 9. Offline mode
- Full form/checklist completion without connectivity; auto-sync when back online (varies — some vendors only cache recent data, others support full offline submission queues)

### 10. Gamification & engagement (less universal, seen in a couple of products)
- Leaderboards, digital "coins"/badges, rep-vs-rep competitions redeemable for rewards

### 11. Integrations
- CRM sync (Salesforce, HubSpot, Zoho, Dynamics 365) and ERP/payroll integration

